;; `assets.clj` is the only reader.
;;
;; Sources, tried in the order `assets/sources` returns:
;;   :hf        Hugging Face; first when a token is configured, skipped when not
;;              (`:is-token-required true`). Credentials never cross the redirect
;;              to HF's CDN.
;;   :pack      the shared Vis assets release - only what Vis exports itself or may
;;              mirror outright. No voice and no GPL data.
;;   :upstream  the publisher: the fallback, and the only source of anything Vis
;;              does not host.
;; Every source of one entry delivers the same bytes, so one `:sha256` covers all.
;;
;; `:needs-espeak-ng true` - each publisher archive carries the GPL-3.0-or-later
;; phoneme tables beside its Piper voice. Vis installs that verified archive into its own
;; model store; it never invokes a package manager or needs administrator privileges.
