  ;; `pocket-voice-clips`, so a new voice never re-publishes 96 MB. An older bundle
  ;; still carries voices/ with three Piper clones; nothing reads them now.
  :license "CC-BY-4.0"
  :attribution
  "pocket-tts by Kyutai (https://huggingface.co/kyutai/pocket-tts), CC BY 4.0, checkpoint b6369a24. ONNX export by the Vis project (bin/export-pocket-tts), published under the same terms with attribution to Kyutai."
  :source-url "https://huggingface.co/kyutai/pocket-tts"
  :notice
  "Pocket speaks by cloning a reference clip. The clips of Kyutai's voice catalogue come in pocket-voice-clips, and any recording can become a voice: `vis-agent speech import <clip.wav> --name <name>`, or POST it to the gateway at /speech/voices. Imported clips stay on the machine that imported them."
  :is-commercial-ok true
  :is-redistributed true
